./library/effect-patterns.md:- Retry: `Effect.retry(schedule)` — Schedule owns count, delay, and `whileInput` predicate. Do not use `Schedule.toStep` as a delay iterator inside `while (true)`.
./contract-work/review2-client.md:**Why this is still a gap.** Architecture §4.1: one Schedule owns `Schedule.recurs(maxGetRetries)` and `whileInput(canRetryAttempt)` for retryable safety classes. VAL-CLIENT-012 only observes PUT 503 then 200 (two fetches). VAL-CLIENT-013’s default 3 / `maxGetRetries: 1` / `HEVY_RETRY_EXHAUSTED` / last `status` is written for GET. VAL-CLIENT-014’s retryable set is “on GET.” VAL-CLIENT-031 only says a *hanging* PUT does not get the free deadline extra attempt. A rewrite that retries PUT at most once, retries PUT without a cap, or skips PUT 429/network, still passes 012 + 031.
./architecture.md:- One attempt is an Effect. The retry driver is `Effect.retry(schedule)` (or equivalent Effect 4 combinator). The Schedule owns:
./architecture.md:  - Delay (`Schedule.addDelay` with existing `getRetryDelayMs`, including Retry-After union + jitter).
